cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DRAgNEt: Deep Research Agent Network for Etymology"
message: "If you use DRAgNEt Case Files, primary-scan proof plates, or verified JSON ledgers in your research, please cite the individual Case File or this repository."
type: dataset
version: "3.1.1"
date-released: "2026-11-25"
authors:
  - family-names: "Callahan"
    given-names: "Joshua"
repository-code: "https://github.com/radbot44/dragnet-etymology"
url: "https://dragnet.tch.one"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >-
  Open-access historical lexicography dataset and AI-authored working-paper archive
  coordinated by Joshua Callahan (DRAgNEt — Deep Research Agent Network for Etymology).
  Publishes machine-validated JSON citation ledgers, verbatim diplomatic transcriptions,
  rejected OCR/misdate leads, and pre-1931 U.S. public-domain newspaper, periodical,
  and court-record scans verified against primary archival repositories, with explicit
  separation between agent_verified, human_verified, and externally_recognized citations.
keywords:
  - etymology
  - historical lexicography
  - antedating
  - American slang
  - archival verification
